From: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] config: enable POWER KVM hosting

The RHEL 9 ppc64le base configuration enables virtualization guest support
but disables the Book3S 64-bit KVM host. Enable the KVM core and its POWER
hypervisor-mode backend as modules so the kernel can also host VMs.
olddefconfig resolves the supporting handlers and dependencies.

This single-setting hunk applies to both the vendor configuration and a
previously resolved configuration, whose surrounding entries differ.

Signed-off-by: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .config | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.config b/.config
--- a/.config
+++ b/.config
@@ -2738 +2738,3 @@
-# CONFIG_KVM_BOOK3S_64 is not set
+# Enable POWER KVM hosting: core and hardware hypervisor backend.
+CONFIG_KVM_BOOK3S_64=m
+CONFIG_KVM_BOOK3S_64_HV=m
